  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "iC8BuSLNh5HjxT/FGF7pzeLM5eQ=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:30:43.257Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Ayesa, including Ibermatica, is marked do-not-pitch, and the reason recorded is size alone: 13,200 people. It was previously ranked first in Spain.\n\nThat is a sequencing judgement rather than a verdict on posture or stack, neither of which was researched. A firm at that scale allocates pilots to practices and evaluates suppliers through procurement, which is the wrong process for shaping something that does not yet have a reference implementation.\n\nThe entry is worth keeping precisely because its exclusion is reversible: what rules it out now is a stage in the go-to-market, not a property of the firm.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**9 \u00b7 do not pitch**\n- Ayesa (incl. Ibermatica) (ES \u00b7 13,200)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> WAS ES #1. Size alone rules it out at this stage.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:30:43.257254Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:30:43.257259Z"
    }
  },
